<h1><span data-field="title" data-format="default">event_type</span></h1>
<p>This <b>read-only</b> variable returns the type of event currently being executed, which can be one of the following constants:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>ev_create</b></li>
<li><b>ev_destroy</b></li>
<li><b>ev_step</b></li>
<li><b>ev_alarm</b></li>
<li><b>ev_keyboard</b></li>
<li><b>ev_keypress</b></li>
<li><b>ev_keyrelease</b></li>
<li><b>ev_mouse</b></li>
<li><b>ev_collision</b></li>
<li><b>ev_other</b></li>
<li><strong>ev_gesture</strong></li>
<li><b>ev_draw</b></li>
</ul>
<p><br/>
For a full list of the constants that are related to the different events see <span class="inline2"><a href="event_perform.htm">event_perform</a></span>, and if you should need the event number (i.e. the sub event), you should be checking the <span class="inline2"><a href="event_number.htm">event_number</a></span>.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-field="title" data-format="default">event_type</span>;</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Constant_Event_Type"><a target="_blank" href="event_perform.htm">Event Type Constant</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">show_debug_message(&quot;Current Event = &quot; + string(<span data-field="title" data-format="default">event_type</span>));</p>
<p>The above code will show a debug message with the event type currently being performed.</p>
<p> </p>
